menu "Application config"

    config EXAMPLE_QSPI_PORT
        int "qspi port"
        default 0
        range 0 1

    config EXAMPLE_QSPI_FREQ_HZ
        int "qspi clock in Hz"
        default 1000000
        range 100000 100000000
        ---help---
            Left low on purpose. With no memory attached there is nothing to keep up with,
            and a slow clock is what makes the trace readable - flying leads and a single
            ground turn a fast bus into crosstalk long before the controller is the problem.

    config EXAMPLE_QSPI_USE_DMA
        bool "use QSPI DMA for payload transfers"
        default n

    config EXAMPLE_QSPI_QUAD
        bool "also issue a transaction with the data phase on four lines"
        default n
        ---help---
            Enable this to issue the four-line payload transaction.  Pin mapping itself
            remains board-owned; on GD32H779V_START IO2/IO3 are PE9 and PE10.

endmenu
